# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal AI Mentor — a local-first mentor on the PI agent harness.
#
# Two runtimes, one boundary: PI (TypeScript) owns the conversation, tools,
# skills and guardrails; `data/` (plain files) is the memory.
#
# The mentor is TypeScript. There is no Python layer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets — the Nebius key lives here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal memory — LOCAL ONLY, never committed.
#
# `data/` holds who he is and what he has done: profile.yaml, memories.jsonl,
# episodes/, schedule/, conversations/, daylog.jsonl. This repository has a
# public remote, so committing it would publish his private life. It is
# deliberately untracked: the files ARE the memory, and they live on his disk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/*` rather than `data/` so the single README can be re-included below —
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded.
data/*
!data/README.md

# Local PostgreSQL data dir (left over from the retired Python layer)
.pgdata/

# Curriculum: recoverable deletions land here (`delete_roadmap` moves a folder in
# rather than unlinking it).
learning/topics/.trash/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored PI agent harness — a separate upstream git repo
# (github.com/earendil-works/pi). Never commit into this repo: it would create
# an embedded repo / huge gitlink.
#
# Also note: PI loads AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md as *project* context, and `pi/` has
# its own build. Keep it out of git; re-clone or rebuild it instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
pi/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.wheels/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Obsidian vault config (docs/ is browsable in Obsidian)
.obsidian/

# IDE & editor
.vscode/
.idea/
.zed/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# The memory agent's own session directory — runtime state, not source.
# (It gets `--session-dir` so it never shares the mentor's session storage.)
.pi/memory-sessions/

